[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"140","stub":{"id":"140","section":"4. Yankee Jims Road Bridge to Lake Clementine","altname":"Shirttail/Ponderosa","river":"American, North Fork","difficulty":"IItoIII","states":["USA-CAL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"878","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"","id":"110921","location":{"latitude":"39.04036676","longitude":"-120.90213504"},"name":"Yankee Jim's Bridge","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"This bridge is probably the most commonly used take out for this section because the river gets considerably easier downstream.","id":"104644","location":{"latitude":"38.99997407","longitude":"-120.93994652"},"name":"Ponderosa Way (take-out)","distance":"4.48","photoID":"0","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"","id":"116188","location":{"latitude":"38.96719886","longitude":"-120.97529545"},"name":"Upper Lake Clementine Beach","distance":"9","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"FlSN3Kxkn7gZQR3wL3Xvf","title":"Yankee Jim's Bridge Closure begins March 17th, 2025","post_date":"2025-02-25 20:03:13+00","detail":"Full notice on the closure is on our main page!","user":{"name":"Jeff Venturino"}}],"photos":[{"id":"1akcO1bi3nEiI36CNXfOM","ext":"jpg","post_id":"DXqub9Yw8n45WZXkJu9dU","description":"A view of the first significant rapid from Yankee Jim's Road. The riverbed splits, the left channel pushing against a wall and creating a pillow that often flips beginners and the right channel dropping steeply over shallow rocks at the end of a pool. Both channels converge to create some fun tail waves at the end. ","caption":"Canyon overlook from the shuttle road","poi_name":null,"subject":"First rapid","author":"trentpearce","poi_id":"110921","photo_date":"2020-03-22T21:16:36.000Z","updated_at":"2021-06-14T21:16:36.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1akcO1bi3nEiI36CNXfOM","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1akcO1bi3nEiI36CNXfOM"}},{"id":"O76UF7Mec7SZVB6jG86Dv","ext":"jpg","post_id":"PVLtA0d1HaMpbAkPiYKOX","description":"Sunset at Yankee Jim's Bridge, the put-in for this run. This is also the take-out for the upstream Chamberlain's Falls section. Note that this area can get incredibly crowded on warm spring weekends and has very limited parking. Plan on arriving early to assure a parking spot. ","caption":"Sunset at Yankee Jim's","poi_name":null,"subject":"Yankee Jim's Bridge","author":"trentpearce","poi_id":"110921","photo_date":"2020-03-22T21:18:51.000Z","updated_at":"2021-06-14T21:18:51.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/O76UF7Mec7SZVB6jG86Dv","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/O76UF7Mec7SZVB6jG86Dv"}},{"id":"S1O6QeKBgSA2GnWI3fSd8","ext":"jpg","post_id":"DpFbk5a7lR3CdSYDo1HMf","description":"Entering the left channel of the first major rapid downstream of the put-in. This drop is visible from the shuttle road. ","caption":"Entering the first rapid","poi_name":null,"subject":"First rapid","author":"trentpearce","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2019-03-21T21:25:02.000Z","updated_at":"2021-06-14T21:25:02.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/S1O6QeKBgSA2GnWI3fSd8","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/S1O6QeKBgSA2GnWI3fSd8"}},{"id":"HOsvYmtclmzS5Z7Mgie5q","ext":"jpg","post_id":"fVPJxgNeA0HM1BoBI8Pnl","description":"Typical scene on the Lower North Fork American. This run flows through a remote and rugged canyon. ","caption":"Typical scene on Lower North Fork","poi_name":null,"subject":"Typical scene","author":"trentpearce","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2019-03-31T21:23:46.000Z","updated_at":"2021-06-14T21:23:46.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/HOsvYmtclmzS5Z7Mgie5q","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/HOsvYmtclmzS5Z7Mgie5q"}}],"detail":{"id":"140","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"This section goes by several names - Ponderosa, Shirttail, and sometimes just 'The North Fork from Yankee Jim down'. A couple of takeout options allow you to choose between about 5 miles on the water to Ponderosa Road Bridge and a longer 9 miles or so to Upper Lake Clementine River Access. It is excellent on a warm, sunny spring day on snowmelt and also often runs in the winter. Upper Clementine is typically subject to seasonal closure so taking out is preferred in the winter/early spring. Rapids are generally Class II between about 800 and 1600cfs. At these flows the most significant features appear in the longer braided rapid visible from Yankee Jim's Road and an excellent and short first-time-boating run can be had between Ponderosa Bridge and Upper Clementine. Above 1500cfs, a few rapids can become a little bit more chaotic. Around 3,000cfs a few holes appear on the run that deserve prudent caution with one notable one appearing about 3 bends below Ponderosa Bridge.\n\nIn 2022 the Ponderosa Road Bridge replacement project necesitated road grading and the takeout road was considerably improved and smooth as of May 2024.\n\n**Put-in:** Colfax-Foresthill Rd.\n\n**Take-out:** Ponderosa Way Bridge (4.5mi) or Upper Lake Clementine Road (9mi)\n\n**CAMPING:** As of 2015, camping is allowed only from 2000’ downstream of Ponderosa Bridge to 1 mile downstream of Codfish Creek. A campfire permit and/or a camp stove permit will be required too.  Also, while they transition into this new policy it would be best to contact and pick up your permits at the [Auburn State Recreation Area](http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=502) office.\n\n**Other information sources:**\n\n- Cassady & Calhoun\n- Holbek & Stanley\n- Martin\n- [California Creeks](http://www.cacreeks.com/amer-nlo.htm)","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"9","correlations":[{"reachID":"140","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"500","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"5000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"NF AMERICAN R A NORTH FORK DAM CA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"11427000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"878","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"1.43","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"38.9359915","longitude":"-121.023802"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/11427000","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/11427000/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"878","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["110921","104644","116188"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-120.90270941,39.04027171],[-120.90273857,39.04011964],[-120.90284586,39.03983632],[-120.90307117,39.03939466],[-120.90308189,39.03913633],[-120.90305651,39.03899652],[-120.90305198,39.03899702],[-120.902964,39.038481],[-120.902915,39.037926],[-120.902961,39.037321],[-120.903124,39.036711],[-120.903299,39.036459],[-120.903436,39.036258],[-120.90364,39.035999],[-120.904105,39.035774],[-120.904586,39.035651],[-120.905195,39.035604],[-120.90597,39.035661],[-120.906554,39.03581],[-120.907266,39.036115],[-